<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon foreground: the company's own VX mark.

  Specification section 3 is explicit that the app must reuse the project's
  official logo rather than invent one, so this is `saarthi_mark.png` — the same
  mark the web app renders — rather than a drawing made for this app.

  ## Getting a landscape mark into a square canvas

  This began as an `<inset>` around the bitmap and looked blurred and cropped,
  and the two attempts at fixing it are worth recording because each failed
  differently:

    * **An inset stretches.** A bitmap drawable fills its bounds, so a 512x307
      mark handed a 64x64 square was squashed into a square and the pin at the
      top read as clipped.
    * **A `center` gravity does not scale.** With the file moved to
      `drawable-nodpi` it decodes at 512px, which on a 3x handset is about
      171dp — far larger than the box — so centring it without scaling simply
      cropped the middle out.

  What works is a box whose *aspect already matches the artwork*: 64x38 is
  512:307 to within a percent, so letting the drawable fill it preserves the
  proportions by construction.

  64dp rather than the 55dp that fits strictly inside the guaranteed 66dp safe
  circle. At 55dp the mark sat visibly small in its tile, and the corners that
  stray past the circle are empty in this artwork — the V and the X do not reach
  them, and the pin sits well inside the left edge. The trade is deliberate: a
  logo nobody can make out is a worse outcome than a transparent corner a round
  mask might clip.

  The file lives in `drawable-nodpi` deliberately. Plain `drawable/` is the mdpi
  bucket, so a 512px image was decoded as though it were 512dp and pre-scaled up
  threefold before being drawn back down — and upscaling then downscaling is
  what softened the fine strokes in the first place.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:gravity="center"
        android:width="64dp"
        android:height="38dp"
        android:drawable="@drawable/saarthi_mark" />
</layer-list>
